  "id": "social-readjustment-rating-scale",
  "term": "Social Readjustment Rating Scale",
  "definition": "The Social Readjustment Rating Scale is a 43-item measure of common life events used to estimate how much social adjustment and stress a person has experienced. It assigns weighted “life change units” to events to reflect the amount of change in usual routine they typically require and to gauge their possible impact on health and well-being.",
